description:
MOA is required to continue Rural Area of Opportunity (RAO) designation from the Department of Commerce. The County must do the following:
1. The County Administrator shall be designated as a point of contact in all matters and activities relating to the Northwest RAO;
2. Kevin Yoder shall serve as the non-profit organization point of contact to represent and provide input on all economic development matters and activities relating to the Northwest RAO;

Adopt an amendment to the 2024-2027 Local Housing Assistance Plan (LHAP) required by the passage of SB 594 to allow Statewide Housing Initatives Partnership (SHIP) grant funds to be expended to relocate residents displaced due to closure of a mobile home park and to allow payment of lot rent for residents of a mobile home park under certain circumstances.
The Affordable Housing Advisiory Committee (AHAC) met monthly from June through September 2026, to review and recommend changes to the 2027-2030 LHAP. A public hearing was held on September 10, 2026, and the AHAC finalized recommendations to be approved by the Board of County Commissioners.
In addition to minor text edits and corrections, the primary changes recommended are as follows:Allow the local government to negotiate a settlement in the event of a disclosure;
Increase in the allowable asset limit from $15,000 to $20,000 per household across all strategies;
Require recipients to hold homeowner's insurance to cover the cost of the SHIP mortgage;

The AHAC is an integral part of the Statewide Housing Initiatives Partnership (SHIP) program. F.S. 420-9076 mandates the committee be composed of 8 to 11 members from actively engaged representatives of the following categories:Residential home building industry;
Banking or mortgage industry;
Home building labor industry;
Advocate for low-income persons;
For-profit provider of affordable housing;
Not-for-profit provider of affordable housing;
Real estate professional;
Citizen of the jurisdiction;
Representative of employers in the jurisdiction;
Representative of essential services personnel;
Actively serving on the local planning committee;
Elected board member.
Seven of the 2025 committee members have agreed to serve on the 2026 AHAC. The returning members represent the following categories:
Regina Hargis-Williams - banking or mortgage industry
Lee Gause - for-profit provider of affordable housing
Kevin Yoder - not-for-profit provider of affordable housing
Joelle Roberts - real estate professional
Kimberly Walters - representative of essential services personnel
Robert Arnold - actively serving on the local planning committee
Jamey Westbrook - elected board member
